@startuml llm-path-local-vs-cloud
title agentd — reaching the LLM: **Local (BYOK)** vs **Cloud (platform keys)**\nSame classes. Same wiring. One flag differs.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #444
  ArrowColor #444
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #999
}

' ─────────────────────────── PRESENTATION ───────────────────────────
package "presentation/" #EAF3FB {
  class Gateway {
    +serve()
    -_handle_conn(ws)
    -_run(handle, message)
    --
    websockets.serve(:8787)
    transport only
  }
}

' ─────────────────────────── APPLICATION ────────────────────────────
package "application/  «no infrastructure imports»" #EEF7EE {
  interface AgentEngine <<port>> {
    +run(messages, system_prompt, tools, model, on_event, abort)
  }

  class AgentService {
    -_engine : AgentEngine
    -_tools
    -_registry
    +handle(message, session_key, agent_id)
    --
    orchestration only:
    load history → prompt → run → persist
  }

  class tool_models <<module>> {
    +brain_model(config) : str
    CONFIG-ONLY
  }
}

' ───────────────────────────── DOMAIN ───────────────────────────────
package "domain/" #FDF6E3 {
  class Message
  class ImageContent
  class AgentSpec
  class AgentEvent
}

' ────────────────────────── INFRASTRUCTURE ──────────────────────────
package "infrastructure/engine/" #FBEEF3 {
  class NativeEngine <<adapter>> {
    -_stream_fn : StreamFn
    -_model : str
    -_model_router
    +run(...)
    --
    run_agent_loop():
    active_model = model_router(model, msgs)
    async for ev in stream_fn(...)
  }
}

package "infrastructure/llm/" #FBEEF3 {
  class CostEfficiencyRouter {
    -text_model
    -vision_model
    +__call__(default_model, messages) : str
    --
    image in outgoing ctx ?
      vision_model : text_model
  }

  class failover <<module>> {
    +make_failover_stream(inner, fallbacks) : StreamFn
    --
    clean error before any output
    → retry next candidate model
  }

  class litellm_stream <<function>> {
    +(model, system_prompt, messages, tools, abort)
    --
    1. messages_to_litellm(...)
    2. build kwargs{model, messages, tools, stream}
    3. model_gateway.apply(kwargs)   ← THE SEAM
    4. await litellm.acompletion(**kwargs)
    5. chunks → text_delta/thinking_delta/
       toolcall_end/done
  }

  class model_gateway <<module>> {
    -_enabled : bool
    -_api_base : str
    -_api_key : str
    +configure(config)
    +apply(kwargs) : dict
    --
    process-wide, set ONCE at boot
  }

  class oneshot <<module>> {
    +text_complete(...)
    +vision_complete(...)
    also calls model_gateway.apply()
  }
}

' ───────────────────────── COMPOSITION ROOT ─────────────────────────
package "main/container.py  «composition root»" #F2F2F2 {
  class build_gateway <<function>> {
    stream_fn = partial(litellm_stream, ...)
    stream_fn = make_failover_stream(stream_fn, fallbacks)
    model_gateway.configure(config)      ← decides the mode
    engine = NativeEngine(stream_fn, brain_model(config),
                          model_router=build_model_router(config))
    AgentService(engine=engine, ...)
  }
}

' ───────────────────────── EXTERNAL / VENDOR ────────────────────────
package "vendor (pip: litellm>=1.60)" #F5F5F5 {
  class "litellm library" as LIB {
    +acompletion(**kwargs)
    --
    model prefix → provider
    reads KEY from os.environ
  }
}

' ══════════════════ THE ONLY DIVERGENCE — SIDE BY SIDE ══════════════
package "◀ LOCAL  (BYOK — default)" #E8F5E9 {
  class ".env on the user's machine" as LOCALENV {
    GEMINI_API_KEY=...
    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
  }
  class "Provider API" as PROV1 {
    generativelanguage.googleapis.com
    api.anthropic.com
  }
}

package "▶ CLOUD  (platform keys)" #E3F2FD {
  class "gateway container\n«separate microservice»" as PROXY {
    litellm[proxy]==1.88.1
    :4000
    --
    litellm.config.yaml:
      model_list: "*" → "*"   (pure passthrough)
    custom_auth.py:
      master key | accounts session token
      AccountsUsageLogger → POST /usage
    --
    holds OUR provider keys
  }
  class "accounts container" as ACCT {
    :4100  /resolve  /usage
  }
  class "Provider API" as PROV2 {
    same providers, our keys
  }
}

' ───────────────────────────── RELATIONS ────────────────────────────
Gateway --> AgentService : delegates chat.send
AgentService o--> AgentEngine : injected «port»
NativeEngine ..|> AgentEngine : implements
AgentService ..> Message
AgentService ..> AgentSpec
Gateway ..> AgentEvent : broadcasts chat.event

NativeEngine --> CostEfficiencyRouter : active_model per iteration
CostEfficiencyRouter ..> ImageContent : trigger to escalate
NativeEngine --> litellm_stream : stream_fn(...)
failover ..> litellm_stream : wraps
litellm_stream ..> Message : messages_to_litellm()

litellm_stream --> model_gateway : apply(kwargs)
oneshot --> model_gateway : apply(kwargs)
litellm_stream --> LIB : acompletion(**kwargs)

build_gateway ..> NativeEngine : constructs
build_gateway ..> AgentService : constructs
build_gateway ..> model_gateway : configure(config)
build_gateway ..> tool_models : brain_model(config)
build_gateway ..> failover : make_failover_stream

' ---- LOCAL tail ----
model_gateway -[#2E7D32,bold]-> LIB : **_enabled = False**\n**kwargs UNTOUCHED**
LIB -[#2E7D32,bold]-> LOCALENV : reads user's key
LIB -[#2E7D32,bold]-> PROV1 : direct HTTPS

' ---- CLOUD tail ----
model_gateway -[#1565C0,bold]-> LIB : **_enabled = True**\nmodel → litellm_proxy/<model>\napi_base → _api_base\napi_key → session token\nuser → account_id
LIB -[#1565C0,bold]-> PROXY : HTTPS (OpenAI wire format)
PROXY -[#1565C0,bold]-> ACCT : GET /resolve (authN)\nPOST /usage (metering)
PROXY -[#1565C0,bold]-> PROV2 : HTTPS with OUR key

note as N1
  **What actually differs between the two modes**
  Exactly one thing: the value of ``model_gateway._enabled``.

  Every class above the seam — Gateway, AgentService, AgentEngine,
  NativeEngine, CostEfficiencyRouter, failover, litellm_stream —
  is byte-identical in both modes and cannot observe which is active.
  That is why "desktop and hosted run the SAME code".
end note

note as N2
  **Model SELECTION is never duplicated.**
  The daemon decides *which* model (brain_model → CostEfficiencyRouter → failover).
  The proxy decides *whether you may* and *who pays* — its model_list is "*" → "*".
  No routing logic exists on both sides.
end note

note as N3
  **"Cloud" ≠ "daemon runs in AWS".**
  A LOCAL desktop daemon that signed in (platform.connect wrote the
  session token to ~/.agentd/.env) takes the BLUE path to the hosted
  gateway container. The switch is BYOK-vs-platform-keys, not where
  the daemon runs.
end note

N1 .. model_gateway
N2 .. PROXY
N3 .. PROXY

@enduml
